# =============================================================================
# apps/web — the ONE env template for the control plane.
# =============================================================================
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
#
# `apps/web/.env.local` is the ONLY env file for apps/web, and the only env file
# in the repo. Next loads it from apps/web; every script, unit test, e2e spec and
# drizzle-kit loads it with `dotenv` from the working directory, which
# `pnpm --filter @kept/web <script>` sets to apps/web. Nothing reads a root
# `.env.local` — delete yours. (Run scripts through pnpm, not from the repo root,
# or dotenv looks in the wrong directory.)
#
# Where else values live:
#   - Railway service variables hold the DEPLOYED values (dev: app.kept-dev.xyz;
#     prod: app.kept.host). No file is deployed.
#   - CI sets its own in .github/workflows/* (GitHub Environment secrets/vars:
#     DATABASE_URL, MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL, R2_*, KV_NAMESPACE_ID,
#     CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CRON_SECRET, RAILWAY_*,
#     NEON_API_KEY, SMOKE_*). docs/prod-release.md §4 is the per-track table.
#   - apps/edge (the Worker) needs NO env file: its vars and bindings are in
#     apps/edge/wrangler.toml, and it holds no secrets.
#
# Rules: never commit a real value here. Anything `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is compiled
# into the browser bundle (and changing it needs a rebuild) — never put a
# secret behind that prefix. Local dev talks to the DEV stores (dev Neon branch,
# dev R2 bucket, dev KV namespace), so local values are the dev track's.
# "openssl rand -base64 32" means: generate a fresh value per track, never
# reuse dev's in prod.
#
# Legend:  [required]  the feature named fails loudly without it
#          [optional]  documented behaviour when unset

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. App & origins
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The control plane's OWN origin — /auth, the studio, /api. The `app.` host,
# never the apex (the apex serves the landing). https locally too: the session
# cookie is `__Host-` prefixed, which requires Secure, and a browser drops a
# Secure cookie over http (sign-in "works", the next request is signed out).
#   local https://localhost:3000 · dev https://app.kept-dev.xyz · prod https://app.kept.host
# [required] middleware host split, claim_url, OAuth fallback origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://localhost:3000

# The suffix pages are served from: {slug}.{KEPT_BASE_DOMAIN}. Bare hostname —
# no scheme, no dot, no slash. Mirrors the Worker var of the same name in
# apps/edge/wrangler.toml. NOT the control plane origin (that is app.{this}).
#   local/dev kept-dev.xyz · prod kept.host
# [required] publish (live_url), purge URLs, host split.
KEPT_BASE_DOMAIN=kept-dev.xyz

# Stops Next's telemetry beacon. On Railway dev it is load-bearing: outbound
# packets keep the service from sleeping. [optional] Next phones home when unset.
NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1

# Where a locked Pro row's CTA links (components/kept/locked-row.tsx). Public
# (it is an href). [optional] unset = locked rows show no link. E11 sets it to
# /founding; leave it unset until then.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCKED_CTA_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Launch gate (lib/launch.ts)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exactly `true` opens publishing and sign-in for everyone. ANYTHING ELSE,
# INCLUDING UNSET, IS CLOSED (the waitlist) — it fails closed on purpose.
#   local true · dev true · prod unset until launch
# Compiled in: changing it needs a rebuild (Railway redeploys on any change).
# `pnpm test:e2e:closed` overrides it to false for the closed specs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEPT_OPEN=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Database (Neon Postgres)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Runtime connection — the POOLED host (`-pooler.` in the hostname).
# How: Neon console → project → Branches → `dev` (prod: the root branch) →
#      Connect → "Connection pooling" ON → copy the postgresql://… string.
# [required] everything that touches the database, including the waitlist.
DATABASE_URL=

# Migrations (drizzle-kit) — the DIRECT host, no `-pooler.`: pooled
# connections cannot take the advisory locks and DDL migrations need.
# How: same Connect dialog with "Connection pooling" OFF.
# [optional] locally, drizzle.config.ts derives it from DATABASE_URL by
# stripping `-pooler.`. Not a Railway variable — CI migrates with its own copy.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Auth (Better Auth + GitHub OAuth + Google OAuth)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Signs sessions and auth tokens. 32+ characters.
# How: openssl rand -base64 32
# [required] sign-in of every kind.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# The origin every OAuth redirect URI is registered against. Keep it identical
# to NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL (local https://localhost:3000). Never the apex, never
# KEPT_BASE_DOMAIN — those hosts serve user HTML.
# [optional] falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://localhost:3000

# GitHub OAuth app, one per origin (a GitHub OAuth app has ONE callback URL, so
# local, dev and prod are three apps).
# How: GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App.
#      Homepage URL: the origin. Authorization callback URL, exactly:
#        local https://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github
#        dev   https://app.kept-dev.xyz/api/auth/callback/github
#        prod  https://app.kept.host/api/auth/callback/github
#      Client ID is shown; "Generate a new client secret" gives the secret.
# [required] the auth module validates all four OAuth values at startup of any
# auth route — sign-in (magic link included) fails without them.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Google OAuth 2.0 client (one client can hold several redirect URIs).
# How: Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen (External;
#      scopes openid email profile only — no verification review) → Credentials
#      → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → "Web application".
#      Authorized JavaScript origin: the origin. Authorized redirect URI, EXACT
#      (a mismatch is an opaque Google error):
#        {BETTER_AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google
#        e.g. https://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
# [required] as above.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Email (Resend) — magic links, draft reminders, waitlist and admin mail
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How: resend.com → Domains → add and verify the sending domain (DKIM + SPF) →
#      API Keys → Create API key → Permission "Sending access", that domain.
#      One account, one 100/day free budget shared by every send.
#      (`pnpm --filter @kept/web resend:tracking` needs a FULL-access key —
#      pass it inline for that one command, don't store it here.)
# [required] every mail; without it sign-in by magic link fails.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Sender, on the verified domain: `page@kept-dev.xyz` or `kept <page@kept-dev.xyz>`.
# [required] with RESEND_API_KEY.
EMAIL_FROM=

# `off` composes and records every mail but skips the Resend call, so a test
# run spends none of the budget. `test:unit` and the Playwright harness set it.
# Honoured ONLY when NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL is localhost; anywhere else it throws.
# [optional] unset (or `on`) delivers. Never set it on Railway.
KEPT_EMAIL_DELIVERY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Storage & edge (Cloudflare R2, KV, cache purge, analytics)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Cloudflare account id — shared by R2 (S3 endpoint) and the KV REST API.
# How: Cloudflare dashboard → any zone's Overview → API → Account ID
#      (or R2 Object Storage → Overview → Account ID).
# [required] publish, replace, delete, manifest writes.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=

# R2 S3 credentials.
# How: Cloudflare dashboard → R2 Object Storage → Manage API tokens → Create
#      API token → Permissions "Object Read & Write" → Specify bucket(s): the
#      track's bucket(s) only → Create. Copy "Access Key ID" and "Secret Access
#      Key" (the secret is shown once).
# [required] publish and every page read the studio does.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# The bucket v1 writes to (sites.region = "auto"). Must match apps/edge/wrangler.toml.
#   local/dev auto-kept-sites-dev · prod auto-kept-sites
# [required]
R2_BUCKET_AUTO=auto-kept-sites-dev
# R2_BUCKET_EU is reserved for E11 (EU residency) and NOT read by any code yet.
# R2_BUCKET_EU=eu-kept-sites-dev

# The manifest namespace the Worker serves from. Not a secret — the same id is
# in apps/edge/wrangler.toml ([env.dev] / [env.prod] kv_namespaces).
# How: Cloudflare dashboard → Storage & Databases → KV → kept-manifest-dev → ID
#      (or `pnpm --filter @kept/edge exec wrangler kv namespace list`).
# [required] every write that changes what a page serves.
KV_NAMESPACE_ID=fd5c0c7fbd9147f4849f65d59cdcd14c

# One API token for KV writes, cache purges and the visits sync. This is NOT the
# deploy token CI uses for wrangler (that one lives in GitHub Environments).
# How: Cloudflare dashboard → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token → Custom:
#        Account · Workers KV Storage · Edit     (KV values PUT/GET/DELETE)
#        Zone    · Cache Purge        · Purge    (purge_cache after writes)
#        Zone    · Analytics          · Read     (GraphQL visits sync, visits:capture)
#      Zone resources: Include → Specific zone → kept-dev.xyz (prod: kept.host),
#      so a dev token can never purge prod. For the local `smoke:cf` script
#      also add Zone · Zone · Read and Zone · DNS · Read.
# [required] KV; without Analytics:Read the visits sync fails on `authz`.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# The zone purged after every manifest write. 32 lowercase hex, not a secret.
# How: Cloudflare dashboard → kept-dev.xyz (prod: kept.host) → Overview → API → Zone ID.
# [optional for a single publish] unset = purge is a logged, non-fatal failure
# and the edge serves the old copy until the repurge cron retries; the visits
# sync needs it.
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Abuse & moderation (scanner, Turnstile, rate limiter, publisher hash)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The page classifier (lib/scan/classifier.ts → OpenRouter decisions API).
# How: openrouter.ai → Settings → API Keys (openrouter.ai/settings/keys) →
#      Create Key → set a monthly credit limit on it.
# [optional] unset = scanner off: scans are recorded `skipped`, only the
# deterministic rule runs, /api/health reports scanner "off".
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare Turnstile — bot check on the waitlist and report forms and on a
# drop-publish from the web client (keyless API publishes carry no token).
# Local and CI: Cloudflare's published TEST keys (below; always pass, and they
# hit the real siteverify endpoint).
# How (dev/prod): Cloudflare dashboard → Turnstile → Add widget → hostnames
#      kept-dev.xyz + app.kept-dev.xyz (prod: kept.host + app.kept.host),
#      Managed → copy the Site Key and the Secret Key.
# [required] unset secret = every token refused (fails closed).
# The site key is public (rendered in the page); the secret is server-only.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA

# Keys the daily salt of lib/rate-limit's per-IP buckets (no IP is stored).
# How: openssl rand -base64 32       (32+ characters)
# [required] magic-link requests, waitlist joins, reports and the keyless
# publish path all hit a limiter and 500 without it.
RATE_LIMIT_SECRET=

# Salt for sites.publisher_hash = sha256(salt, ip, user-agent): dedup and the
# keyless publish governors key on a publisher without keeping its IP.
# How: openssl rand -base64 32
# [required] keyless publish. Rotating it only resets dedup — accepted.
PUBLISHER_HASH_SALT=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Admin & access (closed mode, founding, moderation)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Comma-separated admin addresses (trimmed, lowercased): the ONLY addresses
# that may sign in while closed, the admins of /admin/moderation, and the
# recipients of founding-application and admin-alert mail.
# [optional] unset = nobody is an admin; a closed deploy lets nobody sign in.
KEPT_ADMIN_EMAILS=

# Comma-separated SHA-256 hex digests (64 lowercase hex each) of the
# `kpt_access_…` tokens that may publish while closed. Digests only — the token
# itself never goes in env.
# How: pnpm --filter @kept/web admin:token new
#      prints the token once (hand it to the agent) and its SHA-256; append the
#      digest here / to the Railway variable, comma-separated.
# [optional] unset = no token accepted (admins can still publish signed in).
# A malformed entry throws.
KEPT_ACCESS_TOKEN_HASHES=

# HMAC key for founding one-click review links and waitlist unsubscribe links.
# How: openssl rand -base64 32       (32+ characters)
# [required] waitlist confirm/unsubscribe and founding review.
KEPT_ADMIN_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Cron (/api/cron/*)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bearer secret every /api/cron/* route requires. The schedulers are the
# .github/workflows/cron-*.yml workflows, so the SAME value is also the GitHub
# Environment secret CRON_SECRET (`dev`, and `prod-cron` for prod). Rotate
# Railway first, then GitHub.
# How: openssl rand -base64 32       (32+ characters)
# [required] every cron route (401s otherwise); locally only for the cron tests.
CRON_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Scripts & tests only — leave commented; pass inline when needed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release smoke / canary (`smoke:release`, `seed:canary`; CI sets them from
# GitHub Environment vars). Each also takes a --flag.
# SMOKE_WEB_URL=https://app.kept-dev.xyz
# SMOKE_EDGE_URL=https://smoke.kept-dev.xyz
# SMOKE_LEGAL_PLACEHOLDERS=fail        # fail | warn
# CANARY_STATUS=live                   # seed:canary --status
# VISITS_CAPTURE_DAY=2026-10-03        # visits:capture --day
#
# Set by playwright.config.ts per run — never set these yourself:
#   KEPT_E2E_ACCESS_TOKEN, KEPT_E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL, KEPT_E2E_DRILL_ADMIN_EMAIL,
#   KEPT_E2E_MODERATION_ADMIN_EMAIL, KEPT_E2E_EPIC_ADMIN_EMAIL
# (it also overrides KEPT_ADMIN_EMAILS and defaults RATE_LIMIT_SECRET,
# KEPT_ADMIN_SECRET, the Turnstile test keys and KEPT_EMAIL_DELIVERY=off).
# CI=true is set by the workflows.
